e":3,"verseEnd":70,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"the descendants of Parosh, 2,172; the descendants of Shephatiah, 372; the descendants of Arah, 775; the descendants of Pahath-moab (through the line of Jeshua and Joab), 2,812; the descendants of Elam, 1,254;","from":14},{"book":"EZR","chapter":2,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"the descendants of Bani, 642;","from":14},{"book":"EZR","chapter":2,"verse":11,"verseEnd":12,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"the descendants of Bebai, 623; the descendants of Azgad, 1,222;","from":15},{"book":"EZR","chapter":2,"verse":14,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"the descendants of Bigvai, 2,056; the descendants of Adin, 454; the descendants of Ater (through Hezekiah), 98;","from":16},{"book":"EZR","chapter":2,"verse":17,"verseEnd":70,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"the descendants of Bezai, 323; the descendants of Jorah, 112; the descendants of Hashum, 223; the descendants of Gibbar, 95; the men of Bethlehem, 123;","from":18},{"book":"EZR","chapter":8,"verse":11,"verseEnd":12,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"from the descendants of Bebai, Zechariah son of Bebai, and with him 28 men; from the descendants of Azgad, Johanan son of Hakkatan, and with him 110 men;","from":15}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"28-31":{"people":[{"id":"levi-h3878","name":"Levi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":28},{"id":"moses-h4872","name":"Moses","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Amram","count":1,"firstVerse":29}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H1323","lemma":"בַּת","tr":"bat","gloss":"daughter","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":588},{"base":"H7676","lemma":"שַׁבָּת","tr":"shab·bat","gloss":"Sabbath","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":111},{"base":"H8451","lemma":"תּוֹרָה","tr":"to·rah","gloss":"instruction","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":219},{"base":"H4855","lemma":"מַשָּׁא","tr":"mash·sah","gloss":"interest","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H7668","lemma":"שֶׁ֫בֶר","tr":"she·ver","gloss":"grain","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"H3947","lemma":"לָקַח","tr":"la·qach","gloss":"to take: take","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":966},{"base":"H5411","lemma":"נְתִינִים","tr":"na·tin","gloss":"temple servant","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":17},{"base":"H7605","lemma":"שְׁאָר","tr":"she·ar","gloss":"remnant","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":26},{"base":"H0117","lemma":"אַדִּיר","tr":"ad·dir","gloss":"great","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":27},{"base":"H7621","lemma":"שְׁבוּעָה","tr":"she·vu·ah","gloss":"oath","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":30}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"LEV","chapter":23,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"For six days work may be done, but the seventh day is a Sabbath of complete rest, a day of sacred assembly. You must not do any work; wherever you live, it is a Sabbath to the LORD.","from":31},{"book":"DEU","chapter":7,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Do not intermarry with them. Do not give your daughters to their sons or take their daughters for your sons,","from":30},{"book":"EXO","chapter":23,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"For six years you are to sow your land and gather its produce,","from":31},{"book":"EXO","chapter":23,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"but in the seventh year you must let it rest and lie fallow, so that the poor among your people may eat from the field and the wild animals may consume what they leave. Do the same with your vineyard and olive grove.","from":31},{"book":"EXO","chapter":34,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And when you take some of their daughters as brides for your sons, their daughters will prostitute themselves to their gods and cause your sons to do the same.","from":30},{"book":"NEH","chapter":13,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"In those days I saw people in Judah treading winepresses on the Sabbath and bringing in grain and loading it on donkeys, along with wine, grapes, and figs. All kinds of goods were being brought into Jerusalem on the Sabbath day. So I warned them against selling food on that day.","from":31},{"book":"NEH","chapter":13,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Then I instructed the Levites to purify themselves and guard the gates in order to keep the Sabbath day holy. Remember me for this as well, O my God, and show me mercy according to Your abundant loving devotion.","from":31},{"book":"EZK","chapter":36,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And I will put My Spirit within you and cause you to walk in My statutes and to carefully observe My ordinances.","from":29}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"32-39":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":33},{"id":"levi-h3878","name":"Levi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":4,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"aaron-h0175","name":"Aaron","kind":"person","brief":"High Priest","count":1,"firstVerse":38}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H3881","lemma":"לֵוִי","tr":"le·viy·yi","gloss":"Levi","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":291},{"base":"H4643","lemma":"מַעֲשֵׂר","tr":"ma·a·ser","gloss":"tithe","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":32},{"base":"H3548","lemma":"כֹּהֵן","tr":"ko·hen","gloss":"priest","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":750},{"base":"H3957","lemma":"לִשְׁכָּה","tr":"lish·kah","gloss":"chamber","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":47},{"base":"H8141","lemma":"שָׁנָה","tr":"sha·neh","gloss":"year","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":877},{"base":"H6237","lemma":"עָשַׂר","tr":"a·sar","gloss":"to tithe","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":9},{"base":"H1061","lemma":"בִּכּוּרִים","tr":"bik·kur","gloss":"firstfruit","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":17},{"base":"H3323","lemma":"יִצְהָר","tr":"yits·har","gloss":"oil","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":23},{"base":"H6086","lemma":"עֵץ","tr":"ets","gloss":"tree: wood","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":330},{"base":"H8492","lemma":"תִּירוֹשׁ","tr":"ti·rosh","gloss":"new wine","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":38}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EXO","chapter":13,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"“Consecrate to Me every firstborn male. The firstborn from every womb among the Israelites belongs to Me, both of man and beast.”","from":36},{"book":"DEU","chapter":26,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"you are to take some of the firstfruits of all your produce from the soil of the land that the LORD your God is giving you and put them in a basket. Then go to the place the LORD your God will choose as a dwelling for His Name,","from":35},{"book":"NEH","chapter":13,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"I also arranged for contributions of wood at the appointed times, and for the firstfruits. Remember me, O my God, with favor.","from":34},{"book":"EXO","chapter":23,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Bring the best of the firstfruits of your soil to the house of the LORD your God. You must not cook a young goat in its motherʼs milk.","from":35},{"book":"LEV","chapter":23,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Bring two loaves of bread from your dwellings as a wave offering, each made from two-tenths of an ephah of fine flour, baked with leaven, as the firstfruits to the LORD.","from":37},{"book":"2CH","chapter":2,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Behold, I am about to build a house for the Name of the LORD my God to dedicate to Him for burning fragrant incense before Him, for displaying the showbread continuously, and for making burnt offerings every morning and evening as well as on the Sabbaths, New Moons, and appointed feasts of the LORD our God. This is ordained for Israel forever.","from":33},{"book":"NEH","chapter":13,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"and all Judah brought a tenth of the grain, new wine, and oil into the storerooms.","from":38},{"book":"NEH","chapter":13,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"I appointed as treasurers over the storerooms Shelemiah the priest, Zadok the scribe, and Pedaiah of the Levites, with Hanan son of Zaccur, the son of Mattaniah, to assist them, because they were considered trustworthy. They were responsible for distributing the supplies to their fellow Levites.","from":38}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]}}